hey this is dr. John dallona with Ramsey  Network it's awesome to talk to you  today number one thank you to everybody  who's subscribing to these videos man  the channel is just getting bigger and  bigger and thank you for sending it to  your friends and your family especially  those are talking about racism talking  about anxiety talking about all the  stuff going on in the world today  I appreciate you tuning in and listening  and I'm gonna continue to put out videos  continue to walk alongside you guys  thank you so much today we can take  emails about anxiety about the things  that are troubling each one of you and  then we're gonna get directly into it so  here we go first email up today Scott  asks hey John how's it going good pretty  good doing well I work for my family  business  and during this end-of-the-world phase I  have been working like a madman to make  sure that we stay on our price targets  through this year we were deemed an  essential business but most of our  employees left on their own will we now  have people who have replaced everyone  who left but I kept my foot on the pedal  I was working 70 to 75 hours a week and  last Friday I mentally broke down at  work the family has decided it's in my  best interest to pull back because that  isn't in my blood to do what the rest of  the family does I feel guilty about  leaving them with more of a burden my  question is do you think it's a valid  reason to feel guilty about all of this  at home I have a wife and a  six-month-old baby and I'm just torn up  about what has happened dude Scott thank  you for the email a couple of things  here I want to talk through number one  it's not the end of the world times just  not OK if you go back and read some  literature from a hundred years ago when  the flu pandemic if you read some  literature before that every hundred  years every 50 years every 20 years  there's a big thing a big cage rattling  moment when my dad was a kid it was  coming out of World War two and there  were nuclear weapons pointed at the  United States sitting there in Cuba and  everyone thought the time had come that  this was it my dad had to do nuclear  weapon drills at school as an elementary  school student whoa right so yeah we're  in a mess  millions and millions of people are out  of jobs the United States and the  Western world is having this massive  Awakening  about this tension between who we say we  are and the way we've lived it's very  similar to a lot of us who have said I'm  this kind of person I'm that kind of  person and then we look in the mirror  the last few months we've been stuck at  home and realized no we're not I'm not  as tough as I thought I was I'm not as  strong as I thought I was I am NOT as  ethical as I thought it was I'm not a  great husband like I thought it was all  of us are coming to this this reckoning  and it's really uncomfortable and it's  messy and it's scary so it's not in  thymes and I want everyone to always be  thinking about the light at the other  end of this and what you can do to be  walking towards a light not just  prepping for end times okay those are  for a any specials and for weird  internet chat channels okay so the  second thing here is this good for you  and good for you Scott the world got  crazy and you looked around and said  I've got a family to take care of I've  got a young baby I've got a wife I've  got a family business I've got employees  that work for me I've got a community to  serve and you hit the gas you saw fear  you felt anxiety you got nervous and  then you went in and you were brave and  so I want to applaud you for that I  appreciate your work in your local  community and on behalf of your family  but then comes the other side of that  right you worked 70 75 hours a week you  lost all your employees you hired new  employees back and you kept driving and  driving and driving and then you crashed  so you remember in our anxiety video  your kitchen was on fire right you had  smoke coming out of the oven  you had your countertop was on fire the  roof was on fire everything's burning  and burning and you were running around  making it happen  you kept cooking the meals you kept  making sure people were fed and that  works for a minute if you look around at  the anxiety and the depression and the  ADHD statistics millions and millions  and millions of millions it's almost a  vertical trend line if you look at the  diseases of despair people are dying  from heart disease and liver disease and  addictions and suicides that's this the  United States the Western world our  neighborhoods have been working like  crazy for the last  five 10 20 50 years and we're all at a  breaking point all of our alarms are  going off and we're exhausted and that's  where you found yourself you broke and  we all do you were blessed with a  community with a family who loves you  and said in these moments when you can't  take care of you  we're gonna ask you to step back put  your oxygen mask on get some rest  love that little baby love your wife  recharge and then we'll get you back in  the game it's what a good quarter man  does for a fighter right the quarter man  is there to protect the fighter when the  fighter is just in it and they can't  protect themselves so good for your  family for taking care of you for taking  care of the business at some point your  breakdown breaks down the whole business  right so the question you ask directly  as this is this a valid reason for you  to feel guilty I'm gonna say no you  shouldn't feel guilty but I'm also gonna  tell you feeling guilty is normal I'm  not gonna take that from you okay so are  you feeling guilty yeah you are you  feeling like I should be at work I  should be helping out I should be doing  these things that's natural you're a  fighter you're a good dad you're a good  husband and you're a good businessman so  a better way to frame it is it's normal  to feel guilty but as I just said should  you know k